      "math_academy_id": "e-2566",
      "problem": "Given the diagram shown below, what is the measure of $\\overline{BC}?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14182164/assets/543c7c26c7d56d8ff10f4ece71b74bb5f04edf59fddb6f2c0df549848000abaf.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The segment addition postulate can be applied to a set of more than three collinear points. In the given situation, it states that\n\n$$\nAD = AB + BC +CD.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known values into the equation above, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =AB+BC+CD \\\\ 21 & =5+BC+12 \\\\ 21 & =17+BC \\\\ 21-17 & =BC \\\\ BC & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
